km_s":63,"source":48},3,[65,70,75,80,84,87,91,96],{"met_days":66,"type":67,"label":68,"description":69},0,"launch","Launch — Long March 3B/E","Xichang, China, 2018-12-07. Chang'e 4 — the first spacecraft to soft-land on the lunar far side. Carries the Yutu-2 rover. Required prior deployment of the Queqiao relay satellite at the Earth-Moon L2 point (2018-05) since the far side has no direct line-of-sight to Earth.",{"met_days":71,"type":72,"label":73,"description":74},0.05,"tli_or_tmi","Trans-lunar injection","Long March 3B/E third-stage burn places Chang'e 4 on a direct translunar trajectory.",{"met_days":76,"type":77,"label":78,"description":79},1.19,"tcm","MCC-1","First mid-course correction.",{"met_days":81,"type":77,"label":82,"description":83},2.08,"MCC-2","Mid-cruise refinement.",{"met_days":85,"type":77,"label":86,"description":83},2.97,"MCC-3",{"met_days":88,"type":77,"label":89,"description":90},4.9,"MCC-4 — final pre-LOI","Final approach targeting before lunar orbit insertion.",{"met_days":92,"type":93,"label":94,"description":95},5,"arrival","Lunar orbit insertion","2018-12-12. Captured into a 100 × 400 km lunar orbit. CNSA spent ~22 days adjusting the orbit + waiting for sunlight conditions at the target landing site.",{"met_days":12,"type":97,"label":98,"description":99},"edl_or_oi","Lunar far-side landing — Von Kármán crater","2019-01-03. Powered descent + landing at Von Kármán crater (45.46°S, 177.59°E) inside the South Pole-Aitken basin — first soft landing on the Moon's far side. Yutu-2 rover deployed and is still operating, the longest-lived lunar rover in history.",{"source_tier":101,"parking_orbit":102,"tli":105,"translunar":107,"lunar_arrival":109,"return":111,"waypoints_km":113},"tier_1_5_hybrid",{"altitude_km":103,"inclination_deg":104,"revs":61},200,28.5,{"dv_kms":106},3.15,{"type":108},"direct",{"type":110,"altitude_km":54,"inclination_deg":55,"periselene_km":54},"orbit_and_land",{"type":112},"none",[114,116,117,121,125,128,132,136,139,143,1