r side","The lunar far side has no direct radio line of sight to Earth. To land a spacecraft there, China first launched the Queqiao relay satellite to a halo orbit around Earth-Moon Lagrange point L2 — a vantage point that sees both the far side and Earth simultaneously. With that infrastructure in place, Chang'e 4 became the first spacecraft to soft-land on the far side. The Yutu-2 rover has been operating since January 2019 and has driven ~1.6 km as of 2024, making it the longest-operating lunar rover in history.",[512,516,519,522],{"met":66,"label":513,"note":514,"type":515},"LAUNCH","Long March 3B from Xichang.","nominal",{"met":92,"label":517,"note":518,"type":515},"LOI","Lunar orbit insertion.",{"met":12,"label":520,"note":521,"type":515},"TOUCHDOWN","Lander touches down at Von Kármán Crater 2019-01-03 — first spacecraft on the far side. All comms via Queqiao relay at Earth-Moon L2.",{"met":523,"label":524,"note":525,"type":526},27.01,"YUTU-2 DEPLOYED","Rover rolls down ramp.","info","/orrery/images/missions/change4/07.webp"],"uses":{"params":["id"]}}]}
